  "title": "IPv4: Also allow frames with a good header checksum to pass heuristics",
  "description": "If IPv4 checksum checking is enabled (disabled by default), then allow\nthe IPv4 heuristic dissector to pass IPv4 frames with a different length\nbut where the header checksum is correct. This can happen with frames\nwith Ethernet trailers, among other things.\n\nPrior to 9b4844ed3dd85a95e77c919093b513c217196dbc the GTP dissector\nwould accept frames like this for TPDU heuristics (only using the\nfirst byte for matching), but now it uses the IPv4 heuristic dissector.",
